  "description": "The no-follow regular-file open lives outside the transaction kernel module, where its readers already are.\n\n## Background\n\nThe kernel module exports one helper with consumers outside the transaction path: a capability-relative open that refuses symbolic links and non-regular files. Six call sites use it, five in the JSON storage backend, including the event-log read path, and one in artifact planning. It is the only kernel export that survives the kernel.\n\nMoving it first keeps the kernel's retirement a pure removal.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [hard] REQ-01: The no-follow regular-file open lives in a storage module other than the transaction kernel, with its refusal of symbolic links and non-regular targets unchanged.\n- [hard] REQ-02: Every current call site reaches it at its new home, and it exists in one copy.\n- [hard] REQ-03: Its error type is independent of the transaction kernel's error enum.\n- [hard] REQ-04: Refusal of a symbolic link and of a directory is covered at the storage unit layer.\n",
